WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Operational guardrails help keep LLM API services usable and safe.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:14.655
Input size controls, request limits, rate limiting, quota management, and abuse monitoring protect resources from accidental or deliberate overload.

00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:17.942
These controls are not only for public services.

00:00:17.942 --> 00:00:25.201
Internal automation can loop, retry, or fan out in ways that create surprising cost and resource pressure.

00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:35.336
Prompt injection awareness matters when applications include retrieved documents, user-generated content, tool outputs, or external data in prompts.

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:43.006
Retrieved text should be treated as data to analyze, not as instructions that override the application's policy.

00:00:43.006 --> 00:00:53.757
The API design should separate system instructions, developer constraints, user input, and reference material so the model has a clearer hierarchy to follow.

00:00:53.757 --> 00:00:58.071
Unsafe tool-use boundaries should be handled outside the model.

00:00:58.071 --> 00:01:07.316
If a model suggests an action, the application should validate permissions, scope, data, and policy before anything high impact occurs.

00:01:07.316 --> 00:01:10.603
Model output should not be treated as authority.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:20.464
Structured output should be parsed and validated before use, and high-impact workflows should include human review or additional approval paths.

00:01:20.464 --> 00:01:27.039
Monitoring unusual usage patterns helps identify abuse, misconfiguration, or runaway automation.

00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:36.763
Look for spikes in request volume, unexpected callers, repeated failures, unusual token consumption, suspicious prompts, and high error rates.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:40.666
Content and policy controls should match the application.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:48.473
A customer support assistant, code helper, document reviewer, and automation agent each need different guardrails.
